    "71a379a58529df06fd0ea071bca4302b0a8ccf91": {
      "message": "feat(github): add the GitHub plugin\n\nThe agent side is GitHub's own remote MCP server, mounted through the\nDSH-shipped MCP client, so its tools arrive as mcp__github__*; the human\nside is a right-sidebar tab that follows the Session workspace.\n\n- github.js: origin -> owner/repo, a REST client with a closed set of\n  machine codes, and the write classification the approval relies on\n  (the MCP client keeps no readOnlyHint, so the tool name is the signal).\n- auth.js: imports the gh CLI's OAuth token into the credential store\n  after verifying it, so the row authenticates through\n  ${credential:GITHUB_TOKEN} without a hand-made PAT.\n- index.js: prompt guidance, a tools/pre-execute listener that turns\n  GitHub writes into `ask`, and the prefix route.\n- client: tab registration, repository block, three lists, detail with\n  comment/close/reopen/merge behind a confirm dialog.\n- 78 tests: remote forms, tool classification, REST error mapping, route\n  statuses, the credential bridge, dictionaries, and the built bundle.",
      "author": {
        "name": "litingyes",
        "email": "luz.liting@gmail.com"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "litingyes",
        "email": "luz.liting@gmail.com"
      },
